   "blocks": [
    {
     "type": "key",
     "style": "definition",
     "title": "Relationships",
     "md": "An **entity** is a thing about which data is stored (Customer, Product). Relationships: **one-to-one**, **one-to-many** (one customer places many orders) and **many-to-many** (orders and products), which is resolved with a **link table** holding two foreign keys. An **entity-relationship (E-R) diagram** shows entities and relationships."
    },
    {
     "type": "key",
     "style": "definition",
     "title": "Normal forms",
     "md": "**1NF**: every field holds one atomic value (no repeating groups or lists in a cell) and each record is unique. **2NF**: in 1NF, and every non-key field depends on the **whole** primary key (no partial dependency; relevant for composite keys). **3NF**: in 2NF, and no non-key field depends on **another non-key field** (no transitive dependency). Informally: 'the key, the whole key and nothing but the key'."
    },
